<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 5 June, from 663 to 1968.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">World Environment Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Established by the United Nations in 1972 and observed in over 143 countries, World Environment Day is the principal global platform for raising awareness and driving action on urgent environmental issues.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/changan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/changan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">663 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,363 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Tang court begins moving into the Daming Palace</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under Emperor Gaozong, the Tang imperial family began moving from the Taiji Palace into the new Daming Palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>. It became the seat of the imperial court and the residence of Tang emperors for more than 220 years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozong-of-tang">Emperor Gaozong of Tang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1288">1288 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">738 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John I of Brabant wins the Battle of Worringen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>, Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-duke-of-brabant">John I of Brabant</a>, supported by the counts of Berg and Mark and the citizens of Cologne, defeated and captured Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siegfried-of-westerburg">Siegfried of Westerburg</a>. The victory won Limburg for Brabant, and Cologne became in effect a free city.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-worringen">Battle of Worringen</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-limburg-succession">War of the Limburg Succession</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-duke-of-brabant">John I, Duke of Brabant</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1305">1305 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">721 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bertrand de Got is elected Pope Clement V</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bordeaux">Bordeaux</a> was elected after a long deadlock. Clement V never went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>; his move to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avignon">Avignon</a> began nearly seventy years of papal residence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1832">1832 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">194 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">June Rebellion breaks out in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Republicans raised barricades after the funeral of General Lamarque. The rising was crushed the next day, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-hugo">Victor Hugo</a> later set the climax of Les Misérables on its barricades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1883">1883 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">143 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Express d'Orient makes its first run from Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Georges Nagelmackers's luxury train service left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>. That October it was extended towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, and as the Orient Express it became a legend of rail travel.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Arab Revolt against Ottoman rule begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-bin-ali-king-of-hejaz">Sharif Hussein</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, led by his sons, attacked the Ottoman garrison at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>. Backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, the revolt helped drive the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1947">1947 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">79 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Marshall proposes a plan to rebuild Europe</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a speech at Harvard, the US Secretary of State offered aid to European recovery. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marshall-plan">Marshall Plan</a> provided some $13 billion and deepened the divide between East and West.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Israel launches the Six-Day War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Israeli air strikes destroyed most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s air force on the ground. In six days Israel took Sinai, Gaza, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a>, East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golan-heights">Golan Heights</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert F. Kennedy is shot in Los Angeles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Minutes after winning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> primary, Senator Kennedy was shot by Sirhan Sirhan at the Ambassador Hotel. He died the next day, two months after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> King's assassination.</p></div></li></ol>
